# Adding Hierarchical Filtering to Carbon Intensity Page

## Overview
Add the same Activity → Division → Region hierarchical filtering system from the dashboard to the carbon intensity page. This will provide a consistent filtering experience across the application and allow users to drill down through organizational hierarchy.

## Current State
- Carbon intensity page has a simple year dropdown and facility dropdown
- Facility dropdown shows "All Assets" option
- No hierarchical filtering capability

## Proposed Changes

### [carbon-intensity.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/carbon-intensity.html)

**Replace simple dropdowns with hierarchical filter system:**
- Remove current facility dropdown (lines 473-478)
- Add three cascading dropdown components matching dashboard style:
  - Activity dropdown (EP, LQS, RPC, TRC, All)
  - Division dropdown (filtered by selected activity)
  - Region dropdown (filtered by selected activity + division, with field names)
- Use same glassmorphism styling and dropdown structure as dashboard
- Position filters in top-bar next to year selector

### [carbon-intensity.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/carbon-intensity.js)

**Add filtering logic:**
- Load facilities data from `/api/facilities` endpoint
- Implement cascading filter logic:
  - Activity selection filters available divisions
  - Activity + Division selection filters available regions
- Update all charts and KPIs based on selected filters
- Add field name display in region dropdown options
- Maintain current year filtering functionality

**Functions to add:**
- [updateFilters()](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/dashboard.js#77-134) - Rebuild dropdown options based on current selections
- [renderOptions()](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/public/dashboard.js#135-148) - Generic dropdown option renderer
- `filterData()` - Filter intensity data by activity/division/region
- `refreshCharts()` - Refresh all charts with filtered data

## Implementation Steps

1. Update HTML to add three dropdown components
2. Load facilities data in JavaScript
3. Implement cascading filter logic
4. Update chart rendering to use filtered data
5. Add field name display to region dropdown
6. Test filtering across all charts and KPIs

## Verification Plan

- Test each filter level independently
- Verify cascading behavior (Activity → Division → Region)
- Confirm field names appear in region dropdown
- Ensure charts update correctly when filters change
- Test "All" options at each level
